Method first, in three paragraphs. Paragraph 1 names the model, then the two independent routes that share no library. CAPD (time domain) shows that the cell's first-return map contracts an explicit ball, which certifies a stable orbit. Arb (space-time Fourier) handles the cell and the rings: a radii polynomial in weighted l^1 gives existence and local uniqueness, and one Hill operator plus a Riesz-projection homotopy gives stability. Paragraph 2 gives the results: both cell proofs and the exact link showing they find the same orbit, the N = 8, 16, 32, 64 rotating 1-waves with the period enclosure and the multiplier bound with delta, and the every-N >= 8 and cable family over 73 glued pieces. Paragraph 3 gives the limits: no claim beyond the records, stability only for the cell and those four N, the Hopf identification is numerical, and nothing is claimed for tissue.

Word counts (wc -w): plain 320 (122/158/40), LaTeX 322. Neither counts the keyword and MSC lines, which stay as they are. The 523 figure for the current abstract is wc -w of .tex lines 51-55, and that range includes keywords and MSC.

The LaTeX compiled cleanly (exit 0) when I appended it to the paper's own preamble (lines 1-49) in the scratchpad. It uses \re, which line 32 of the paper defines. I edited no file. Neither version contains an em dash; Tusscher--Panfilov uses an en dash.

